# Port Azura

**Port Azura** is an original open-world crime mini-game built in Three.js for the **make.fun gta6-01 bounty**. You are Rico Vale, a broke marina courier in a sun-soaked coastal city, working a 4-mission story chain for fixer Marina Sol: meet the fixer, steal back her gold Comet, lose the Azura PD heat, and win a timed pier showdown against the Violet Vipers — while pedestrians flee, traffic rolls, and a 1–5 star wanted system keeps the police ramming your bumper.

## Features
- Procedural coastal city: road grid, varied buildings, sidewalks, palms, streetlights, beach, marina, boats and a pier
- On-foot third-person play + steal/drive/exit any car; traffic and parked cars
- Wanted system (1–5 stars), police pursuit/ramming, busted & wasted states, wanted decay when hidden
- Hitscan pistol combat, rival gang shooters, pier target dummies, health for player/NPCs/cars
- 4-mission story with dialogue, cash rewards, win state, and localStorage save/continue
- HUD with health, cash, wanted stars, objective text and a live 2D minimap
- WebAudio-synthesized SFX (engine, siren, gunshots, chimes, thuds) + synth music loop
- Keyboard/mouse and mobile touch controls (virtual joystick + buttons)

## Controls
- **WASD / Left stick** — move / drive
- **Mouse / drag right side** — camera look
- **Shift** — run
- **E / ENTER button** — enter/steal car, exit car
- **F or Left-click / FIRE button** — shoot
- **Space** — handbrake (driving) / jump (on foot)
- **P / Esc** — pause · **M** — mute

Run locally with `node serve.ts`, then open http://localhost:8080.
